   "id": "b01",
   "text": "1879. Edison invents the *light bulb.*",
   "frames": 154
  },
  {
   "id": "b02",
   "text": "Nope. *Not exactly.*",
   "frames": 66
  },
  {
   "id": "b03",
   "text": "Edison: *the light bulb myth.*",
   "frames": 66
  },
  {
   "id": "b04",
   "text": "Electric light was *already* around.",
   "frames": 95
  },
  {
   "id": "b05",
   "text": "In the early 1800s, Humphry Davy made *arc lights.*",
   "frames": 137
  },
  {
   "id": "b06",
   "text": "Blindingly bright. *Not for your living room.*",
   "frames": 107
  },
  {
   "id": "b07",
   "text": "*Dozens* of inventors tried to make a bulb.",
   "frames": 110
  },
  {
   "id": "b08",
   "text": "In England, *Joseph Swan* showed one before Edison.",
   "frames": 129
  },
  {
   "id": "b09",
   "text": "The problem? They *burned out* fast.",
   "frames": 93
  },
  {
   "id": "b10",
   "text": "Edison's team tested *thousands* of materials.",
   "frames": 120
  },
  {
   "id": "b11",
   "text": "Their carbon filament lasted *much longer.*",
   "frames": 111
  },
  {
   "id": "b12",
   "text": "Later, bamboo bulbs lasted over *1,000 hours.*",
   "frames": 136
  },
  {
   "id": "b13",
   "text": "Edison also built the *whole system.*",
   "frames": 95
  },
  {
   "id": "b14",
   "text": "Power stations. Wires. *Meters.*",
   "frames": 100
  },
  {
   "id": "b15",
   "text": "And Swan? Edison *sued* him.",
   "frames": 83
  },
  {
   "id": "b16",
   "text": "Then they *teamed up* instead.",
   "frames": 75
  },
  {
   "id": "b17",
   "text": "Their company was called *Ediswan.*",
   "frames": 99
  },
  {
   "id": "b18",
   "text": "Edison made the bulb *practical.* He didn't invent it.",
   "frames": 121
  },
  {
   "id": "b19",
   "text": "Inventors of the light bulb: *way more than one.*",
   "frames": 119
  },
  {
   "id": "b20",
   "text": "Anyway, here's Edison inventing the *light bulb.*",
   "frames": 134
  }
